4025-/*
4026- *  #326: the record forms. Every floating-point instruction that defines an
4027- *  Rc bit gets a `_dot` twin here, generated by FDOT: run the base, then set
4028- *  CR field 1 from FPSCR[0:3].
4029- *
4030- *  fcmpu and mcrfs are absent ON PURPOSE. Neither defines Rc -- the low bit
4031- *  of their encoding is reserved -- so there is no `fcmpu.` or `mcrfs.` to
4032- *  implement, and an encoding with that bit set is invalid rather than a
4033- *  record form. The decoder keeps rejecting those two.
4034- */
4035-FDOT(frsp)
4036-FDOT(fctiw)
4037-FDOT(fctiwz)
4038-FDOT(fneg)
4039-FDOT(fabs)
4040-FDOT(fnabs)
4041-FDOT(fmr)
4042-FDOT(fsel)
4043-FDOT(fadd)
4044-FDOT(fsub)
4045-FDOT(fmul)
