8822-B.7.1 Operations on Doublewords
8823-
8824-All these mnemonics can be coded with a final " . " to cause the Rc bit to be set in the underlying instruction.
8825-
8826-Table 9. Doubleword rotate and shift mnemonics
8827-
8828-Operation                            Extended Mnemonic                     Equivalent to
8829-                                                                           rldicr ra,rs,b,n- 1
8830-Extract and left justify immediate   extldi ra,rs,n,b (n > 0)              rldicl ra,rs,b+n,64- n
8831:                                                                           rldimi ra,rs,64- (b+n),b
8832-Extract and right justify immediate  extrdi ra,rs,n,b (n > 0)              rldicl ra,rs,n,0
8833-                                                                           rldicl ra,rs,64- n,0
8834-Insert from right immediate          insrdi ra,rs,n,b (n > 0)              rldcl ra,rs,rb,0
8835-                                                                           rldicr ra,rs,n,63- n
8836-Rotate left immediate                rotldi ra,rs,n                        rldicl ra,rs,64- n,n
8837-                                                                           rldicl ra,rs,0,n
8838-Rotate right immediate               rotrdi ra,rs,n                        rldicr ra,rs,0,63- n
8839-                                                                           rldic ra,rs,n,b- n
8840-Rotate left                          rotld ra,rs,rb
8841-
8842-Shift left immediate                 sldi ra,rs,n (n < 64)
8843-
--
8851-
8852-                                     Appendix B. Assembler Extended Mnemonics 151
8853-                                                                                                        Version 2.01
8854-
8855-Examples
8856-
8857-1. Extract the sign bit (bit 0) of register Ry and place the result right-justified into register Rx.
8858-
8859-extrdi Rx,Ry,1,0                                   (equivalent to:             rldicl Rx,Ry,1,63)
8860-
8861-2. Insert the bit extracted in (1) into the sign bit (bit 0) of register Rz.
8862-
8863:insrdi Rz,Rx,1,0                                   (equivalent to:             rldimi Rz,Rx,63,0)
8864-
8865-3. Shift the contents of register Rx left 8 bits.
8866-
8867-sldi Rx,Rx,8                                       (equivalent to:             rldicr Rx,Rx,8,55)
8868-
8869-4. Clear the high-order 32 bits of register Ry and place the result into register Rx.
8870-
8871-clrldi Rx,Ry,32                                    (equivalent to:             rldicl Rx,Ry,0,32)
8872-
8873-B.7.2 Operations on Words
8874-
8875-All these mnemonics can be coded with a final " . " to cause the Rc bit to be set in the underlying instruction. The
8876-operations as described above apply to the low-order 32 bits of the registers, as if the registers were 32-bit regis-
8877-ters. The Insert operations either preserve the high-order 32 bits of the target register or place rotated data
8878-there; the other operations clear these bits.
8879-
8880-Table 10. Word rotate and shift mnemonics
8881-
8882-Operation                            Extended Mnemonic                              Equivalent to
8883-                                                                                    rlwinm ra,rs,b,0,n- 1
8884-Extract and left justify immediate   extlwi ra,rs,n,b (n > 0)                       rlwinm ra,rs,b+n,32- n,31
8885:                                                                                    rlwimi ra,rs,32- b,b,(b+n)- 1
8886:Extract and right justify immediate  extrwi ra,rs,n,b (n > 0)                       rlwimi ra,rs,32- (b+n),b,(b+n)- 1
8887-                                                                                    rlwinm ra,rs,n,0,31
8888-Insert from left immediate           inslwi ra,rs,n,b (n > 0)                       rlwinm ra,rs,32- n,0,31
8889-                                                                                    rlwnm ra,rs,rb,0,31
8890-Insert from right immediate          insrwi ra,rs,n,b (n > 0)                       rlwinm ra,rs,n,0,31- n
8891-                                                                                    rlwinm ra,rs,32- n,n,31
8892-Rotate left immediate                rotlwi ra,rs,n                                 rlwinm ra,rs,0,n,31
8893-                                                                                    rlwinm ra,rs,0,0,31- n
8894-Rotate right immediate               rotrwi ra,rs,n                                 rlwinm ra,rs,n,b- n,31- n
8895-
8896-Rotate left                          rotlw ra,rs,rb
8897-
8898-Shift left immediate                 slwi ra,rs,n (n < 32)
--
8904-Clear right immediate                clrrwi ra,rs,n (n < 32)
8905-
8906-Clear left and shift left immediate  clrlslwi ra,rs,b,n (n  b < 32)
8907-
8908-Examples
8909-
8910-1. Extract the sign bit (bit 32) of register Ry and place the result right-justified into register Rx.
8911-
8912-extrwi Rx,Ry,1,0                                   (equivalent to:             rlwinm Rx,Ry,1,31,31)
8913-
8914-2. Insert the bit extracted in (1) into the sign bit (bit 32) of register Rz.
8915-
8916:insrwi Rz,Rx,1,0                                   (equivalent to:             rlwimi Rz,Rx,31,0,0)
8917-
8918-3. Shift the contents of register Rx left 8 bits, clearing the high-order 32 bits.
8919-
8920-slwi Rx,Rx,8                                       (equivalent to:             rlwinm Rx,Rx,8,0,23)
8921-
8922-4. Clear the high-order 16 bits of the low-order 32 bits of register Ry and place the result into register Rx,
8923-    clearing the high-order 32 bits of register Rx.
8924-
8925-clrlwi Rx,Ry,16                                    (equivalent to:             rlwinm Rx,Ry,0,16,31)
8926-
